+# Attempt account: evaluation of the actual response
+
+The preceding response work supplied exact residual identities and named the
+actual moments N0,N1,N2 without evaluating them. This continuation attacked
+those integrals through the differentiated original vacuum equation rather
+than introducing another abstract source model. The SU(2) commutator square
+supplies a pointwise logarithmic-derivative bound, and the original vertex
+Casimir supplies a bounded inverse on the actual covariant derivative source.
+
+The first local drift has an explicit remainder independent of the exterior
+box. That makes it possible to calculate the neighboring-plaquette contribution
+in its original Haar coordinates and return it to the actual interacting
+vacuum with finite errors. The result encloses all three moments and a
+positive-shift Schur response, together with the restored norm. The exact
+coupling and loop-size domains remain in A14, A25–38 and A46–51.
+
+The proof audit corrected the last cohomological identification: the local
+trial is not asserted to be the metric-minimizing section. A45a gives the
+actual canonical section and the full positive section-correction term. The
+numerical response bounds are unchanged, and the checker now rejects the
+uncorrected quotient-norm identity on an explicit rational example.
+
+The narrow evaluated interval is a controlled large-g result; it supplies a
+nonzero actual forcing and a quantitative test of the response machinery.
+The all-coupling results also apply to the retained running path, but with
+their actual growth factors. The physical zero-shift response and the full
+singlet energy margin remain unevaluated. No conclusion about the continuum
+mass lower edge has been substituted for those quantities.
